from assessment import add, save

add('6537',1990,'circa','Estimated origin of the unrestricted word-RAM linear-time sorting frontier around the fusion-tree era. Integer sorting is older; the card retains arbitrary word length, randomization and one uniform program rather than a fixed-width radix-sort task.',('random','deterministic','course'))
add('6510',1962,'circa','The cubic APSP barrier dates to the Floyd–Warshall era in 1962. A fixed polynomial improvement is the later standard formulation of that longstanding speedup question; the modern fine-grained conjecture is newer.',('upper','equiv'))
add('6783',2013,'circa','Estimated origin of the specific four-additive, four-thirds-size target around the 2013 four-additive-spanner constructions. Additive spanners are older; the survey and later papers record the remaining exponent gap.',('primary','upper2025','barrier'))
add('0388',1976,'by','Fredman’s 1976 paper explicitly attributes the X+Y sorting problem to Berlekamp, so the question was already posed by then. The comparison bound is not an algorithm with the running-time guarantee requested here.',('fredman','primary'))
add('7380',2014,'year','The 2014 Towards (1+epsilon)-Approximate Flow Sparsifiers paper asks for size depending only on the terminal count and approximation error. This dates the approximate multicommodity version, not older exact terminal sparsification.',('agk',))
add('0946',2018,'by','The cited 2018 open-problem entry records the optimal linear-in-vertices hypergraph cut-sparsifier target. Graph cut sparsification is older; its history does not establish the first date of this hypergraph bound.',('primary',))
add('7350',2020,'by','The output-sensitive near-linear target is explicitly recorded in the 2020 Top-k-Convolution paper. Classical pseudopolynomial Subset Sum and the original decision problem are much older.',('primary',))
add('7233',1962,'circa','The fixed-base-below-two question is anchored to the 1962 Bellman and Held–Karp dynamic programs. Modern bit-model and bounded-error conventions refine that old exact weighted-TSP speedup problem.',('recent','tradeoff'))
add('6662',2006,'circa','The deterministic restricted-isometry construction problem emerged with compressed sensing in the mid-2000s. Strauss posed a related weaker-row-count milestone in 2006; the optimal row count on this card is the stronger modern target.',('strauss2006','road','bourgain'))
add('4790',1974,'circa','The classical meet-in-the-middle algorithm of Horowitz and Sahni in 1974 is the historical anchor for beating the one-half exponential exponent. The card’s bounded-error uniform model specifies the surviving algorithmic question.',('primary',))
add('5705',2024,'year','The small-class conjecture is explicitly Conjecture 9 in the 2024 paper. It is a replacement for the older factorial-growth implicit-graph conjecture refuted in 2022, not the same conjecture with an older birth date.',('primary','small-2025'))
add('2018',2024,'year','The 2024 submodular-hypergraph sparsification paper poses this quadratic support-size target. Earlier ordinary graph and hypergraph sparsification problems are precursors with different cut models.',('primary',))
add('3346',2020,'by','The 2020 source records the vertex-parameterized quasipolynomial hypergraph-isomorphism question. This target separates dependence on the vertex count from the explicit input length, unlike the older general graph-isomorphism question.',('primary',))
add('6785',2000,'circa','Estimated origin in the late-1990s/early-2000s study of additive spanners with genuinely linear size. The numerical exponent for each fixed edge coefficient is the atlas’s later precision convention for that tradeoff.',('primary','lower-2022'))
add('1012',1997,'circa','Estimated origin of the efficient capacity-achieving binary list-decoding challenge in the 1990s algorithmic list-decoding program. List decoding itself was introduced in the 1950s; the deterministic binary construction demanded here is a later stronger objective.',('primary','survey'))
add('7358',1980,'circa','Estimated origin in the first wave of polynomial-time approximation algorithms for graph Steiner Tree around 1980. The optimization problem is older; the exact best randomized approximation ratio and 0.01 precision are later formulations of its approximability frontier.',('lp','hardness'))
add('0809',2013,'year','Erickson explicitly posed the strongly polynomial improvement target in the 2013 planar-optimization seminar report. Minimum-cost flow itself predates this particular planar running-time question.',('primary',))
add('6421',2015,'year','The cited 2015 paper poses a general isomorphism dichotomy for hereditary graph classes. This card selects finitely forbidden classes, a concrete restriction of that broader direction.',('primary',))
add('6784',2006,'year','The target asks whether spanners can match the sublinear-error emulator tradeoffs of Thorup and Zwick’s 2006 work. Spanners and emulators allow different edge sets, so the emulator theorem is the origin of the comparison, not a solution.',('emulators','primary'))
add('7075',1990,'circa','Approximate date for the general minimum-cardinality vertex-connectivity augmentation frontier, studied by the late twentieth century. The survey records the unresolved unrestricted-target case; fixed connectivity and increasing connectivity by one are older related variants.',('primary','fpt-2026'))
add('7351',2010,'by','Chan and Patrascu’s 2010 paper records inversion counting as a central word-RAM complexity frontier. Counting inversions is classical; this date is a documented anchor for the linear-time machine-model target, not the invention of the statistic.',('primary','hardness'))
add('1141',2026,'by','The cited 2026 paper explicitly records this near-linear constant-factor target for reachability diameter, which ignores unreachable ordered pairs. Older directed-diameter questions use related but sometimes different conventions.',('current','preprint'))
add('1338',2026,'year','Conjecture 23 of the 2026 paper asks to remove all logarithmic factors from the chain-length support bound. This particular set-system formulation is new relative to classical graph sparsification.',('primary',))
add('5969',1981,'circa','Estimated origin around the early-1980s complexity classification of three-edge-coloring in general graphs. The planar restriction survives separately; cubic bridgeless planar graphs are governed by the older four-color connection.',('primary','journal-2026'))
add('6173',2023,'by','The directed three-pair individually-shortest-path question is explicitly open in the 2023 source and again in 2026. Disjoint paths and undirected shortest-path variants are older; their first dates are not assigned to this precise directed question.',('primary','dsp-2026'))
add('3263',1995,'circa','Estimated origin of the fixed-k minimum-total-length refinement around the 1990s fixed-k disjoint-paths breakthrough. The 2021 source records the optimization gap; minimizing the total length differs from requiring every path to be individually shortest.',('primary','cycles2025'))
add('7061',2020,'by','The general edge-deletion dichotomy direction is recorded in the 2020 survey. The atlas specializes it to finite forbidden induced-subgraph families; older vertex-deletion dichotomies do not give the same statement.',('primary','journal'))
save()
